  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration**\nThe data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` has 14,074 requests from 1,001 unique client IPs. Its time field is `timestamp`, and `@timestamp` holds the same values. The `response` field has three codes: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), and 503 (441). The top destination countries are CN, IN, and US.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-b8bd6761 Web logs overview\"**\nDashboard ID `eff-b8bd6761-web-logs-overview-07238ae5002c`, with six panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Unique client IPs (metric)\n- Average response size in bytes (metric)\n- Requests over time by response code (line, top 5 codes)\n- Requests by response code (pie)\n- Top countries by requests (bar, top 10)\n\nI set the time range to 2026-01-01 through 2027-01-01. The sample data runs to 2026-12-03, which is after today (2026-10-11), so a range ending at \"now\" would hide most of it.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-b8bd6761 5xx spike\"**\nRule ID `12ea65c9-cd5e-429c-aa82-2c2b2b4dbc6c`. It is an `.es-query` rule in `stackAlerts`, with these settings:\n- Runs every 1 minute.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5??` on `timestamp` over the last 5 minutes.\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- Enabled, with status \"pending\" because it hasn't run yet.\n\nChoices I made that you didn't specify:\n- The rule has no connector actions, so it records alerts but doesn't notify anyone. Tell me if you want an action attached, such as a server log or Slack.\n- Matching uses a wildcard on `response.keyword` rather than a numeric range, because `response` is stored as a string.\n\nThe rule is unlikely to fire on the existing sample data. The 503 responses are spread across October through December, so a 5-minute window will rarely hold more than 10 of them unless new 5xx events are arriving.\n\nOne gap: `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` isn't set in my shell, so I couldn't call the raw REST API directly. I used the Kibana MCP tools for all writes and checked the results through those tools and ES|QL.",
